WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
A mug, made of ceramic.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.730
A drinks bottle, made of plastic.

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.970
A bike frame, made of carbon fibre.

4
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.730
Why not swap them around?

5
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.810
Would a ceramic bike frame work?

6
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.150
Does it even matter?

7
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.630
Are these materials all much the same?

8
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.930
In this mission, you'll meet
three kinds of material: ceramics,

9
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.790
polymers and composites.

10
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.050
You'll find out what
each one is made from.

11
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.430
You'll see what each one is
good at, and where it fails.

12
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.090
Then you'll meet a material
made by combining two others.

13
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.620
Your mission: explain why each
object is made from its material.
